WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.586
Hello.

2
00:00:00.586 --> 00:00:09.278
Some equations do not separate at once, but one clever substitution makes them separable.

3
00:00:09.278 --> 00:00:14.552
Today we meet one such kind, the homogeneous equation.

4
00:00:14.552 --> 00:00:21.974
Its signature: if you zoom the picture, the direction field does not change.

5
00:00:21.974 --> 00:00:29.006
By the end you will confidently use the substitution y equals u times x.

6
00:00:29.256 --> 00:00:36.921
If multiplying x and y by the same number t leaves the right side unchanged,

7
00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:41.258
the function is homogeneous of degree zero.

8
00:00:41.258 --> 00:00:46.805
Then the right side depends only on the ratio y over x.

9
00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:49.125
Put y equals u times x.

10
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:54.975
By the product rule y prime equals u prime times x plus u.

11
00:00:54.975 --> 00:01:01.934
We get x times u prime equals phi of u minus u, a separable equation.

12
00:01:02.184 --> 00:01:08.360
Example: y prime equals x squared plus y squared over x times y.

13
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:15.984
Numerator and denominator both have degree two, so the equation is homogeneous.

14
00:01:15.984 --> 00:01:23.414
Dividing top and bottom by x squared gives phi of u equals one over u plus u.

15
00:01:23.664 --> 00:01:31.440
Substitute y equals u times x: u prime times x plus u equals one over u plus u.

16
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:37.543
The u terms cancel, leaving x times u prime equals one over u.

17
00:01:37.543 --> 00:01:43.251
This is never zero, so there is no straight-line solution.

18
00:01:43.251 --> 00:01:46.598
Separate: u d u equals d x over x.

19
00:01:46.848 --> 00:01:54.569
Integrate: one half of u squared equals the natural logarithm of the absolute value of x plus C one.

20
00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:58.198
Put back u equals y over x and multiply by two.

21
00:01:58.198 --> 00:02:08.467
The answer is y squared equals x squared times the entire quantity in parentheses: two natural log of the absolute value of x plus C.

22
00:02:08.467 --> 00:02:12.250
The parentheses and absolute value are essential.

23
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:16.574
Always write the final answer in the original variables.

24
00:02:16.824 --> 00:02:25.961
Look at the direction field: along every ray from the origin the segments have the same slope.

25
00:02:25.961 --> 00:02:30.335
That is the geometric meaning of homogeneity.

26
00:02:30.335 --> 00:02:39.278
So stretching or shrinking one integral curve about the origin gives another integral curve.

27
00:02:39.528 --> 00:02:46.480
Check question: if y equals u times x, what is y prime?

28
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.766
Remember the product rule.
